{
  "slug": "swiftui-guidance-for-macos",
  "name": "Swiftui Guidance For Macos",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Runtime-level SwiftUI guidance for macOS apps. Covers observation internals, concurrency scheduling, view identity, performance, AppKit bridging, SwiftData, and accessibility — with deep explanations of why patterns work, not just what to do. Built from developing a production macOS browser with SwiftUI and from reading the Swift runtime source. Targets macOS 26+, Swift 6.2 with strict concurrency. Designed for frontier models: skips basics, focuses on non-obvious traps and mechanisms that even experienced developers get wrong.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **1 skill**, `swiftui-macos` (Expert SwiftUI guidance for macOS apps — covers writing and reviewing code with runtime-level understanding of observation, concurrency,…).\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install swiftui-guidance-for-macos@claude-community` from `kageroumado/swiftui-macos-skill`.",
